---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Local SEO in Sioux Falls, SD | Couch & Craft"
description: "Show up on Google Maps when Sioux Falls searches for what you do. Google Business Profile, local SEO and a monthly report."
crumb: "Marketing"
service:
  name: "Local SEO and Google Business Profile"
  type: "Local search marketing"
  description: "Google Business Profile, local SEO, review requests and call tracking for Sioux Falls service businesses."
---
<section class="page-hero band--navy" aria-labelledby="page-heading">
  <div class="container page-hero__inner flow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Marketing</p>
    <h1 id="page-heading">Show up when {{ site.business.city }} searches for what you do.</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__sub">Most of your calls start with a Google search or a Maps listing. I work on both, then show you each month what came in.</p>
    <p class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--gold" href="/start/" data-track="cta_click" data-label="marketing-hero">Start a project</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="included-heading">
  <div class="container flow" style="--flow-space: var(--space-l)">
    <h2 id="included-heading">What I work on</h2>
    <dl class="included">
      <div class="included__row">
        <dt>Google Business Profile</dt>
        <dd>The listing that shows up on Maps and on the right side of a search. Hours, photos, services and the service area all need to be right, or Google shows someone else.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="included__row">
        <dt>Local SEO</dt>
        <dd>Making sure your site says, in plain words, what you do and which towns you work in. That's how Google matches you to a search like "roofer in Brandon."</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="included__row">
        <dt>Review requests</dt>
        <dd>A simple way to ask happy customers for a Google review after the job. Real reviews from real customers. I'll never write one for you.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="included__row">
        <dt>Call and form tracking</dt>
        <dd>So you can see which calls and form fills came from your site and your listing, not just guess.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--white" aria-labelledby="report-heading">
  <div class="container report-section">
    <div class="flow">
      <h2 id="report-heading">The report you'll get every month</h2>
      <p>One page. What came in, where it came from and what I did. If something isn't working, it says so.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/start/">Start a project</a></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="report" aria-labelledby="report-caption">
      <figcaption id="report-caption" class="report__label">Sample report. Numbers are made up to show the layout.</figcaption>
      <div class="report__sheet">
        <header class="report__head">
          <p class="report__business">Sample Roofing Co.</p>
          <p class="report__month">Monthly report · September</p>
        </header>
        <dl class="report__stats">
          <div><dt>Calls from Google</dt><dd>34 <span class="report__change">up 6</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Form leads</dt><dd>11 <span class="report__change">up 2</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Maps views</dt><dd>1,920</dd></div>
          <div><dt>New reviews</dt><dd>4</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="report__cols">
          <div>
            <h3 class="report__subhead">Top searches</h3>
            <ol class="report__list">
              <li>roofer sioux falls</li>
              <li>roof repair near me</li>
              <li>hail damage roof brandon sd</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="report__subhead">What I did</h3>
            <ul class="report__list">
              <li>Added 12 job photos to the Google listing</li>
              <li>Wrote a page for storm damage repair</li>
              <li>Fixed the hours shown on Maps</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="report__next"><strong>Next month:</strong> ask last month's customers for reviews.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="care-heading">
  <div class="container care">
    <div class="flow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Care &amp; Growth plan</p>
      <h2 id="care-heading">{{ site.pricing.careMonthly | open }} a month</h2>
      <p>For owners who want someone keeping an eye on the site and the listing after launch.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="checklist__list">
      {%- for item in site.carePlan.includes %}
      <li>{{ item | open }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="band band--white">
  <div class="container">
    {%- set faqs = [
      { q: "Do I need a new website first?", a: "<p>[JUSTIN TO SET: whether the Care &amp; Growth plan works with a site you didn't build]</p>" },
      { q: "Will you write reviews for me?", a: "<p>No. Fake reviews break Google's rules and they read fake to customers too. I'll help you ask real customers, at the right time, in a way that's easy for them.</p>" },
      { q: "Can I cancel?", a: "<p>[JUSTIN TO SET: cancellation terms for the Care &amp; Growth plan]</p>" }
    ] -%}
    {% set faqId = "marketing-faq" %}
    {% include "partials/faq.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

